from pathlib import Path
import json
H=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
r=json.loads((H/'results.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
lines=['# Distant supernova spectra: acquisition and readiness audit','','Ten reduced, calibrated ESO ESSENCE DR3 spectra are cached with SHA-256 hashes and verified FITS checksums. These include six supernova extractions, three host-galaxy extractions and one combined extraction, covering five identified supernovae. They are development observations, not untouched outcomes. No spectral ages have been fitted.','','## Provenance and version selection','','The live ESSENCE ObsCore query returns 185 rows: 184 explicitly named v3.0 and one older v2.0 entry. Selection uses exact catalog identities and v3.0 filenames, not temporal coincidence. The published Narayan et al. 2016 catalog supplies the IAU aliases and heliocentric redshifts. Its served table is pipe-delimited; parsing checks all 422 records.','','The ESO datalink response returned an Internal error for b027. The documented public dataPortal/file/<dp_id> endpoint succeeded. Full FITS headers remain in the cached originals. The results manifest preserves all download URLs and hashes, selected archive rows, units and timing metadata.','','## Acquired observations','','| Object / extraction | Midpoint MJD (UTC) | Observer wavelength (Angstrom) | Archive SNR/pixel | Difference from nearest published same-object epoch (days) |','| --- | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: |']
for x in r['spectra']:
 lo,hi=x['wavelength_range_angstrom'];dt=x['midpoint_minus_published_days']
 lines.append(f"| {x['catalog_identity']['iau_name']} / {x['target']} | {x['mid_mjd']:.8f} | {lo:.1f}-{hi:.1f} | {x['header']['SNR']:.2f} | {dt:+.6f} |")
q=[x for x in r['spectra'] if x['target']=='q106'];q.sort(key=lambda x:x['mid_mjd']);span=q[1]['mid_mjd']-q[0]['mid_mjd']
z=float(q[0]['catalog_identity']['z_host']);rest_hi=min(x['wavelength_range_angstrom'][1] for x in q)/(1+z)
lines+=['','## What this enables', '',f'SN 2006mk (ESSENCE q106) has two SN spectra separated by **{span:.6f} observer days**. Both midpoints agree with the corresponding rounded published dates within 0.005 day. Host redshift is 0.4754 +/- 0.0001 in the catalog. Its common upper rest-wavelength coverage is approximately {rest_hi:.1f} Angstrom: the 4000-5500 Angstrom development window fits within both spectra, while 4000-7000 does not. Valid coverage does not guarantee usable spectral features or an unbiased age estimate.','','For reference, applying the known wavelength definition lambda_rest=lambda_observed/(1+z) changes spectral coordinates, not observing dates. Applying an event-duration factor of 1+z would instead be a hypothesis under test: this pair would correspond to %.3f source days if that hypothesis holds, versus %.3f days for unchanged arrival intervals. Neither number is a newly measured spectral age. Do not divide the dates before fitting.'%(span/(1+z),span),'','## Data issues retained','','- WAVE values, TUNIT1=angstrom and primary WAVELMIN/MAX in nm consistently imply Angstrom-valued arrays. TCOMM1 says nm and is inconsistent. The code checks numerical endpoint consistency explicitly; it never uses that comment for conversion.','- SPECSYS=BARYCENT and the release documentation describe barycentric wavelength correction. These are not source-rest-frame arrays. The catalog redshifts are heliocentric; resolve the frame convention before precision template comparisons.','- All arrays have finite positive per-pixel errors, but no full interpixel covariance is supplied in these three-column products. Extraction/resampling can correlate errors; diagonal errors alone are not a complete likelihood.','- The archive labels FLUXCAL=ABSOLUTE, while the release describes relative flux calibration; TOT_FLUX is false. Do not treat these spectra as calibrated total supernova brightness. Slit losses, host subtraction and linked photometry must enter a joint brightness model.','- SN 2002iz and b027 midpoint discrepancies (0.0085 and 0.0125 days) exceed simple two-decimal date rounding. Retain both dates and investigate provenance rather than forcing agreement. SN 2003js differs by 0.602 days, so its acquired observation must not be substituted for the listed paper epoch.','- E142/D093 alias documentation contains a contradictory E132 reference. That additional possible epoch is excluded pending position and provenance checks. SN 2006sc has no exact r190 target in this release selection.','- Repeated GAL/SNGAL extractions of an exposure are not independent temporal observations. The six SN spectra do not provide six independent supernova aging slopes.','','## Next calculation','','Specify a reproducible continuum/host treatment and wavelength-frame transformation; degrade object-excluded nearby templates to the actual resolution, coverage and error characteristics; calibrate phase recovery before estimating the 2006mk observer-time aging slope. Obtain missing epochs and matched photometry. This acquisition is input readiness, not a redshift/timing/brightness solution. All six goals remain open.','','## Sources and attribution','','- ESO DR3 announcement: https://www.eso.org/sci/publications/announcements/sciann17686.html','- Release description: https://www.eso.org/rm/api/v1/public/releaseDescriptions/225','- DOI: https://doi.org/10.18727/archive/22','- Catalog: https://cdsarc.cds.unistra.fr/viz-bin/ReadMe/J/ApJS/224/3?format=html&tex=true','- Published epoch comparison: https://arxiv.org/html/0804.3595v1#S3.T2','- Documented download endpoint: https://archive.eso.org/programmatic/HOWTO/jupyter/query-ancillary-files/query-ancillary-files.html','','Data are from ESO programs 170.A-0519 and 176.A-0319 (PI Bruno Leibundgut), ESSENCE release DOI above. Preserve ESO CC BY 4.0 attribution and the per-product REFERENC bibliography when publishing any derived science.','']
(H/'report.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines),encoding='utf-8')
print({'sn2006mk_observer_span_days':span,'conditional_stretched_source_span_days':span/(1+z),'files':len(r['spectra'])})
